<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simone de Beauvoir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1908">1908</a>–<a href="/years/1986">1986</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Simone Lucie Ernestine Marie Bertrand de Beauvoir, Castor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simone de Beauvoir was a French existentialist philosopher, writer, social theorist and feminist activist with a significant influence on feminist existentialism and feminist theory. In 1929 she was placed second in the agrégation in philosophy, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-paul-sartre">Jean-Paul Sartre</a>, at 21 the youngest person to pass it. Her <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-second-sex">The Second Sex</a> (1949), a detailed analysis of women's oppression, became a foundational tract of contemporary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feminism">feminism</a>. She also wrote the novels She Came to Stay (1943) and The Mandarins (1954), and memoirs beginning with Mémoires d'une jeune fille rangée (1958); she received the 1954 Prix Goncourt and the 1975 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> Prize.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simone-de-beauvoir.jpg" alt="Simone de Beauvoir" width="330" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moshe Milner · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simone_De_Beauvoir_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in 6th arrondissement of Paris, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in 14th arrondissement of Paris, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.85,2.33&amp;year=1958" aria-label="6th arrondissement of Paris on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4604 458 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Simone de Beauvoir"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5054 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.85,2.33&amp;year=1958">What was here in 1958? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
